Id: cron010w
Severity: WARN
Category: cron
Check: check_crontabs
Fix: Delete the orphaned crontab, unless it is for an account still to come.
References: crontab(5), cron(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

The cron spool holds a crontab named after an account that does not
exist: one deleted without its crontab, or a file put there by hand.
cron ignores it for now, but the moment an account of that name is made
(a new employee with an old user name, an account restored from a
backup) cron runs it as that account, with whatever it says.

Read it, and delete it unless it is meant for an account still to come.
